+## The combined fix set (2026-11-04, `zz-column-fixes.mysql.sql`)
+
+The three lanes' findings were merged and de-duplicated; the migrations that were proven became ONE additive file and the code changes ONE patch.
+The file is a finishing pass: it constrains tables other migrations create, so it is named to sort last, it is the last install part, and
+`db-schema-diff.mjs` keeps any `zz-*.mysql.sql` last when it shuffles migration orders.
+
+| step | what | why |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | `order_items.name_en/name_ar` varchar(120) to varchar(160), collation kept | a product named 121-160 characters made every order that contains it answer HTTP 500 under strict sql_mode |
+| 2 | `products.brand_slug` varchar(64) to varchar(80) | `brands.slug` is 80 |
+| 3 | `products.updated_at` | the sitemaps ask for it for `<lastmod>` and never found it |
+| 4 | `customer_accounts.birthday`, `birthday_set_at`, `birthday_sent_year`, `last_login_at` | the birthday feature and the Profiles "last sign-in" were off on any database built from `dropin/php-store` |
+| 5 | `product_variants` UNIQUE (`slug`, `size`) | a second row for one size made it unbuyable (409 out_of_stock) |
+| 6 | six named CHECKs: money >= 0, discount percent <= 100 | `?r=sync` stored a negative price and an order accepted it as a discount nobody configured |
+
+Every step that existing rows could refuse (5 and 6) counts the offending rows first and, if there are any, skips only that step with one printed
+line; a step whose table or column is missing is skipped the same way. Importing the file twice changes nothing.
+
+The code patch (`admin.php`, `store.php`, `customer.php`, both payment callbacks, `crm.mysql.sql`, `make-install-sql.mjs`, the privacy inventory
+and the two audit tools) is independent of the migration in both directions: every use of a new column is guarded or needs none. Order of work on the
+live database: read-only schema diff job, backup, the pre-check counts at the top of the migration (all 0), import, the schema diff job again.
+
